Adaptation_method:
Avoid multiple calls to `.parse()` when `storeOptionsAsProperties: true`, or disable the option and access parsed values via `.opts()`. Example:

Before:
```js
program.storeOptionsAsProperties(true);
program.parse(process.argv);
program.parse(['--port', '3000']); // throws in v13
```

After:
```js
// Option 1: Use .opts() instead (recommended)
program.storeOptionsAsProperties(false);
program.option('--port <number>');
program.parse(process.argv);
const opts = program.opts();

// Option 2: Parse only once and avoid subsequent .parse() calls
program.parse(process.argv);
// Do not call .parse() again
```
